{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game concept game concept","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md","fileName":"Game Concept.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Concept","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Design Methods]] · [[Game Concept Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Game Concept Development","Second-Order Design","Play Space","Game Idea","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game concept game concept","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md","fileName":"Game Concept.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Concept","heading":"Game Concept","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game concept is the single driving idea that unifies what players do, how they progress, and what the experience is meant to feel like. It provides a shared reference for selecting systems, content, theme, and style.\n\nA focused concept does not prescribe one player path. It guides [[Second-Order Design]] by defining the intended whole while leaving room for a broad [[Play Space]] and discovery through prototyping.\n\nFor commercial discussion, a game concept must be detailed enough to identify the player's role and primary activity, audience, genre, platform, business model, competition modes, progression, world, and broad story direction. It is more developed than a [[Game Idea]] but remains an outline rather than a complete design.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Game Concept Development","Second-Order Design","Play Space","Game Idea","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game concept game concept","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Concept.md","fileName":"Game Concept.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Concept","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Game Concept Development","Second-Order Design","Play Space","Game Idea","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}